{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-136875" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=4 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=-3\\end{aligned}\\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}20 & a & 10 \\\\ c & 80 & -20 \\\\ 10 & -20 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}22 \\\\ b \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations and its corresponding normal equation shown above. What is the value of $a-b+c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071217/state.json" "file_sha256" "f19cd6c504b26047c6e1f0bd7d5bd81e01500ec9105516223f9b130e5d3a6e87"} {"question" "q-136875" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write our system in matrix form as $Ax=b,$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -8 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe normal equation corresponding to $Ax=b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -8 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & -8 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -8 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}20 & -40 & 10 \\\\ -40 & 80 & -20 \\\\ 10 & -20 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}22 \\\\ -44 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\na-b+c=(-40)-(-44)+(-40)=-36.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071217/state.json" "file_sha256" "f19cd6c504b26047c6e1f0bd7d5bd81e01500ec9105516223f